<h3 dir="auto">Description</h3>

<p dir="auto">JPEG-XL is now supported in Firefox Beta and Developer Edition (found out through my own testing).</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Motivation</h3>

<p dir="auto">This will allow readers to be informed about the state of the format's support, which is relevant because of the data savings the format can enable.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Additional details</h3>
<p dir="auto">Since Firefox 152 Stable has not come out yet, I'm not sure if its row should be filled out or left blank, but the other rows should definitely be updated since the versions in those rows (Beta and Developer Edition) have been released.</p>

<h3 dir="auto">Related issues and pull requests</h3>
<p dir="auto">None that I could find.</p>



